      "message": "[1]: I didn\u0027t check `dawn_weverything \u003d false` before and test building it fail without these additional -Wno- flags.\n\nThese cflags are moved from `src/dawn/common/BUILD.gn` from the `config(\"internal_config\")` (which include \"src/utils:internal_config\" -\u003e \"dawn_warnings\")\n\nSo I don\u0027t get whey they used to build but now they require explicit -Wno- flags here to suppress, instead of suppressing in their own config (e.g. cflags +\u003d [ \"-Wno-c2y-extensions\" ] is in src/dawn/common/BUILD.gn)\n\nDoes the order of these clang flags potentially impacting ending result? (order -Wpandetic and -Wno-) \n\nOn the other hand we have many to triage later, so I wonder if it\u0027s okay to land it like this now and work further on new CLs.",
