      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ahh yes the flag ordering is probably the issue. Testing in godbolt, `-Wall` overrides earlier `-Wno-*`, it probably expands to a list of `-W*` flags which undo any past `-Wno-*` for the same warning. (In contrast, `-Weverything` doesn\u0027t reset previous flags. They\u0027re just handled a bit differently.)\n\nThe GN rules for flag ordering are here:\nhttps://gn.googlesource.com/gn/+/main/docs/reference.md#variables-you-set-in-targets-cflags_flags-passed-to-the-c-compiler_back-to-top-ordering-of-flags-and-values-1\n\nThe only way to fix this in GN would be to move any suppressions into a `config` so it gets added later. Hopefully we can avoid that entirely by using `--warning-suppression-mappings` instead and avoiding suppressing any warnings anywhere other than `dawn_warnings`. I just [tested it](https://godbolt.org/z/5hbfzso6x) and it seems to be fine (not sensitive to flag order).\n\nAnyway yes I think this is fine.",
